        "original_id": "baa3316e-7648-5721-bd04-183daa731b68",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Hodge, Danny Boyle, Irvine Welsh, Alex Garland\n- Works: Trainspotting, Shallow Grave, A Life Less Ordinary, The Beach, The Final Curtain, Alien Love Triangle, T2 Trainspotting, Porno\n- Roles: screenwriter, dramatist, director, novelist\n\nFacts:\n- John Hodge was born in 1964 and is a British screenwriter and dramatist.\n- John Hodge is most noted for adapting Irvine Welsh's novel \"Trainspotting\" into the screenplay for the film \"Trainspotting.\"\n- John Hodge wrote the film \"Shallow Grave\" in 1994.\n- John Hodge wrote the film \"Trainspotting\" in 1996.\n- \"The Beach\" is a 2000 British-American adventure drama film directed by Danny Boyle.\n- \"The Beach\" is based on Alex Garland's 1996 novel of the same name and was adapted for film by John Hodge.\n- John Hodge wrote the film \"A Life Less Ordinary\" in 1997.\n- John Hodge wrote the film \"The Beach\" in 2000.\n- John Hodge wrote \"The Final Curtain\" in 2002.\n- John Hodge wrote the short film \"Alien Love Triangle\" in 2002.\n- \"T2 Trainspotting\" was directed by Danny Boyle and written by John Hodge.\n- \"T2 Trainspotting\" is based on characters created by Irvine Welsh in his novels \"Trainspotting\" and \"Porno\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
